     {
      "type": "TextualBody",
      "purpose": "describing",
      "value": "Across nine experiments, reminders of money (vs neutral primes) induced a self-sufficient orientation: primed participants requested less help, helped/donated less, and preferred to work, play, and stand apart from others.",
      "language": "en"
     }
    ],
