     {
      "type": "TextualBody",
      "purpose": "describing",
      "value": "Green & Tao prove the primes contain arbitrarily long arithmetic progressions, via three ingredients: Szemeredi theorem (positive-density integer subsets contain arbitrarily long progressions), a new TRANSFERENCE PRINCIPLE extending it to positive-relative-density subsets of pseudorandom sets, and a Goldston-Yildirim result placing the primes in a pseudorandom set of almost primes.",
      "language": "en"
     }
    ],
    "target": [
     {
      "type": "SpecificResource",
      "source": "https://shir-openu.github.io/meta-tagging-showcase/papers/greentao2004-primes.html",
      "selector": {
       "type": "TextQuoteSelector",
       "exact": "We prove that there are arbitrarily long arithmetic progressions of primes. There are three major ingredients. The first is Szemer ́edi's theorem",
       "prefix": "random set of almost primes. - \"",
       "suffix": "... The second, which is the mai"
      }
     },
