      "type": "TextualBody",
      "purpose": "describing",
      "value": "Relevant information in X about Y is extracted by squeezing X through a bottleneck of codewords that preserves maximum information about Y — a variational principle generalizing rate-distortion theory, with distortion emerging from the joint statistics of X and Y.",
      "language": "en"
     }
    ],
    "target": {
     "type": "SpecificResource",
     "source": "https://shir-openu.github.io/meta-tagging-showcase/papers/tishby1999-information-bottleneck.html",
     "selector": {
      "type": "TextQuoteSelector",
      "exact": "we squeeze the information that X provides about Y through a 'bottleneck' formed by a limited set of codewords ̃X. This constrained optimization problem can be seen as a generalization of rate distortion theory in which the distortion measure d(x, ̃x) emerges from the joint statistics of X and Y .",
      "prefix": "joint statistics of X and Y. - \"",
      "suffix": "\" finding The method yields an e"
     }
    }
   },
